rearms","confidence":0.95,"rationale":"The bill directly restricts firearm sales and possession for individuals subject to extreme risk orders, affecting manufacturers and dealers."},{"industry":"ideological-single-issue","confidence":0.85,"rationale":"Advocacy organizations focused on gun rights, gun safety, and civil liberties have direct stakes in extreme risk protection order legislation."},{"industry":"legal","confidence":0.7,"rationale":"The bill creates new federal court petition procedures and legal processes for contesting orders, generating demand for legal representation."}],"plainSummary":"This bill would allow family members and law enforcement to ask federal courts to temporarily prohibit someone from buying or possessing firearms if that person poses a danger to themselves or others. It would make it a federal crime for individuals subject to these orders to have guns, require the FBI to track such orders nationwide, and provide grants to help states and tribes create or enforce similar laws. The bill sets out procedures for issuing, contesting, and renewing these temporary restrictions.","classificationMethod":"llm","plain":{"whoItTouches":"People caught up in the criminal law, and victims of crime.","confidence":"crs-summary"},"topOverlap":{"bioguideId":"C001091","score":0.03343276735938982},"overlapCount":109},"meaning":{"percentile":31.55071777882947,"median":0.01073720309570498,"n":6339,"ordinary":[],"unattributedShare":0.7507326509255339}}],"votes":[{"id":"a64a90b759595d68f3a8d502","billId":"119-hr-7008","date":"2026-07-22T16:51:00-04:00","question":"Yea-and-Nay","result":"Passed","position":"Yea","sourceUrl":"https://clerk.house.gov/evs/2026/roll280.xml"},{"id":"2afa499bcaceefdcecfa862a","billId":"119-hr-8800","date":"2026-07-22T16:37:00-04:00","question":"Yea-and-Nay","result":"Passed","position":"Nay","sourceUrl":"https://clerk.house.gov/evs/2026/roll278.xml"},{"id":"e69a4fe10a0cc4e4d35ffc3d","billId":"119-hr-6955","date":"2026-07-21T22:05:00